1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,820
Segun went all the way

2
00:00:00,820 --> 00:00:02,900
to Aba because of Amaka.

3
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:04,220
You see this love thing?

4
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:05,540
The party was big,

5
00:00:05,540 --> 00:00:07,020
the speakers were loud,

6
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:08,220
all members of the family

7
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:09,400
were present.

8
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:11,420
He paid a bride price,

9
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:12,980
the traditional rites were

10
00:00:12,980 --> 00:00:13,760
done.

11
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:14,780
After that,

12
00:00:14,780 --> 00:00:15,800
they were recognised and

13
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:16,860
seen as Mr.

14
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:17,620
and Mrs.

15
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:18,440
Odukoya.

16
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:19,740
But are they validly married

17
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:20,860
under the law?

18
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:22,000
Welcome to another edition

19
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:22,860
of Fast Law Friday,

20
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:24,700
and today we'll discuss:

21
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:26,620
is customary marriage valid,

22
00:00:26,620 --> 00:00:28,280
and what are the differences

23
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:30,680
between a customary marriage

24
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:32,480
and a statutory marriage?

25
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:34,060
The simple answer to whether

26
00:00:34,060 --> 00:00:35,780
a customary marriage is

27
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:37,980
valid under the law is

28
00:00:37,980 --> 00:00:38,880
yes.

29
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:40,520
Section 32 of the Marriage

30
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:42,280
Act expressly preserves

31
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:44,220
marriages contracted under

32
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:46,500
customary rites and customs.

33
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:47,680
For a customary marriage to

34
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:48,620
be valid,

35
00:00:48,620 --> 00:00:49,560
there are certain elements

36
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:50,760
that need to be featured.

37
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:51,680
Consent of both parents,

38
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:53,880
consent of both parties,

39
00:00:53,940 --> 00:00:55,520
payment of bride price and

40
00:00:55,520 --> 00:00:56,680
its acceptance,

41
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:58,240
most importantly,

42
00:00:58,240 --> 00:00:59,680
performance of traditional

43
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:00,080
rites,

44
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:01,820
which differs from place to

45
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:02,460
place,

46
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:03,320
culture to culture,

47
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:04,420
and lastly,

48
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:05,760
handing over of the bride

49
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:07,180
to the groom.

50
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:08,240
Now here it is.

51
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:09,400
How is customary marriage

52
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:11,080
different from statutory

53
00:01:11,080 --> 00:01:12,120
marriage?

54
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:13,600
One of the major

55
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:14,640
distinctions between

56
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,300
customary marriage and

57
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:17,820
statutory marriage is the

58
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:19,560
law that governs it.

59
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:20,980
Customary marriage is

60
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:22,750
governed by customs and

61
00:01:22,700 --> 00:01:25,020
traditions of a particular

62
00:01:25,020 --> 00:01:25,500
culture,

63
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:26,840
whilst statutory marriage is

64
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:27,740
governed by the Marriage

65
00:01:27,740 --> 00:01:28,560
Act.

66
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:29,620
However,

67
00:01:29,780 --> 00:01:31,440
cultural traditions differ

68
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:33,020
from place to place.

69
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:33,520
The check,

70
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:34,960
or the balance in it,

71
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:36,500
is that those customs and

72
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:37,980
traditions must not be

73
00:01:37,980 --> 00:01:39,060
repugnant to natural

74
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:40,140
justice,

75
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:42,180
equity and good conscience.

76
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:43,320
Another major distinction

77
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:44,820
between customary marriage

78
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:46,340
and statutory marriage is

79
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:47,880
that customary marriage is

80
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:48,820
mostly polygamous,

81
00:01:48,820 --> 00:01:51,340
while statutory marriage is

82
00:01:51,340 --> 00:01:52,880
strictly monogamous.

83
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:53,760
As a woman,

84
00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:54,680
if you intend to have

85
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:56,760
a monogamous marriage,

86
00:01:56,760 --> 00:01:58,000
doing a customary marriage

87
00:01:58,000 --> 00:01:59,220
alone might not be the

88
00:01:59,220 --> 00:02:00,320
best option for you.

89
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:00,880
You might need to go

90
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:02,220
the extra mile of doing

91
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:03,660
a statutory marriage.

92
00:02:03,660 --> 00:02:04,360
Lastly,

93
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,520
divorce and dissolution of

94
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:06,340
marriage.

95
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:07,960
Under customary law,

96
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:09,480
it engages a less strict

97
00:02:09,480 --> 00:02:10,800
procedure,

98
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:12,500
such as returning of the

99
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:14,100
bride price or the family

100
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:15,220
dissolving the marriage

101
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:17,300
amongst themselves.

102
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:18,080
However,

103
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:19,780
under statutory marriage,

104
00:02:20,920 --> 00:02:22,400
it is guided by the

105
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:22,790
Matrimonial Causes Act,

106
00:02:22,790 --> 00:02:25,280
where the marriage is

107
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:27,200
dissolved in a court of

108
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:28,700
competent jurisdiction.

109
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:29,840
Nowadays,

110
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:31,520
we have people that do

111
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:33,380
both customary marriage and

112
00:02:33,380 --> 00:02:35,200
statutory marriage together.

113
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:36,400
It is necessary for you

114
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:37,260
to know that the moment

115
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:38,360
you do both marriages,

116
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:39,520
the statutory marriage

117
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:40,920
supersedes the customary

118
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:42,280
marriage that you have done,

119
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:43,420
which means that the

120
00:02:43,420 --> 00:02:44,340
Marriage Act and the

121
00:02:44,340 --> 00:02:45,880
Matrimonial Causes Act are

122
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:48,200
more binding on you than

123
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:49,300
customary law.

124
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:49,760
With this,

125
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:50,660
I believe you can make

126
00:02:50,660 --> 00:02:52,380
a better decision on which

127
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:53,280
marriage to do:

128
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:55,600
customary or statutory.

129
00:02:55,740 --> 00:02:56,740
Thank you.

